{%- comment -%}
  tonescan-landing
  ----------------
  Code-first, dark, professional SaaS landing page for the tonescan app.
  Rendered via templates/page.tonescan.liquid using layout/tonescan.liquid
  (real shop logo + theme fonts; no shop header/footer).

  CONVENTIONS:
  - Tailwind v4, prefix-first: tw:flex, tw:md:grid, tw:hover:opacity-90.
  - Dark theme. Accent = BLUE: #3b82f6 (buttons/dots/borders), #60a5fa (eyebrow text).
  - MINIMAL corner radius: tw:rounded-[2px] on cards/frames/buttons/tiles/badges (pro-software vibe).
    rounded-full ONLY on tiny indicator dots.
  - Container matches the main site: max-w-[1400px], px-[15px] md:px-[50px] (logo click doesn't jump).
  - Arbitrary PX for type/spacing (theme root is 62.5%). Layout utils (flex/grid) are safe.
  - COPY RULE: sell tangible benefits, never the tech stack. RGB trichromatic support is the
    key differentiator — it leads.
  - Content is plain inline HTML — edit copy directly.
  - Status: OPEN BETA (free now; perpetual + subscription at launch). "(soon)" = not shipped.
  - Scroll reveal + hero parallax wired in layout/tonescan.liquid (fails safe).
  - Placeholders in [ brackets ] / grey boxes: screenshots, testimonials, prices, real social proof.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="tonescan-landing tw:text-neutral-200">

  {%- comment -%} ============================ 1 · HERO ============================ {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    GitHub-style hero: a COLOURFUL region (.ts-hero-color, blue gradient) whose bottom edge is a
    SHARP CUT to the page's black (#0a0a0b). The framed screenshot dips past that cut so its dark
    bottom melts into black ("cut off"), and the feature SELECTOR (.ts-hero-selectbar) sits on the
    black part below. Desktop = tab pills; mobile = a <select> + pagination dots, screenshot bleeds
    off-screen wider than the viewport, and no grow-on-scroll.
    overflow-clip (not hidden) so the sticky hero text still pins while floats / wide image stay clipped.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="tw:relative tw:overflow-clip">
    <div class="tw:pointer-events-none tw:absolute tw:left-1/2 tw:top-[-160px] tw:h-[360px] tw:w-[720px] tw:-translate-x-1/2 tw:rounded-full tw:bg-white/[0.04] tw:blur-[130px]"></div>

    <div class="ts-hero-color">
      <div class="ts-hero tw:relative tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:px-[15px] tw:pt-[80px] tw:pb-0 tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:pt-[120px]">
        {%- comment -%}
          Floating sample images — scattered high around the headline, then drift DOWN and inward
          to the screenshot centre (rack into focus) on scroll. --drop tunes how far down they
          travel to reach the hero centre. Swap gradients for real sample scans later.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="hero-floats tw:hidden tw:md:block" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="hero-float hero-float--1"></div>
          <div class="hero-float hero-float--2"></div>
          <div class="hero-float hero-float--3"></div>
          <div class="hero-float hero-float--4"></div>
          <div class="hero-float hero-float--5"></div>
          <div class="hero-float hero-float--6"></div>
          <div class="hero-float hero-float--7"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ts-hero-text tw:mx-auto tw:flex tw:max-w-[860px] tw:flex-col tw:items-center tw:gap-[26px] tw:text-center">
          <h1 class="tw:text-[42px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.03] tw:tracking-[-0.03em] tw:text-white tw:md:text-[72px]">
            Pro-grade film colour, effortless workflow.
          </h1>

          <p class="tw:max-w-[600px] tw:text-[18px] tw:leading-[1.55] tw:text-neutral-400 tw:md:text-[20px]">
            Turn whole rolls of camera-scanned negatives into gallery-ready photos —
            with lab-accurate colour, effortlessly.
          </p>

          <div class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:flex tw:flex-wrap tw:items-center tw:justify-center tw:gap-[12px]">
            <a href="#signup" class="ts-dl-btn tw:inline-flex tw:items-center tw:justify-center tw:rounded-[2px] tw:bg-[#3b82f6] tw:px-[26px] tw:py-[14px] tw:text-[15px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white tw:transition-transform tw:hover:-translate-y-[1px]">
              Join the beta
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ts-hero-frame tw:relative tw:mx-auto tw:mt-[120px] tw:max-w-[1320px] tw:md:mt-[180px]">
          <div class="ts-hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          {%- comment -%} glass frame + stacked feature shots (crossfaded by the selector below).
             Bottom is open (no bottom border) and dips past the colour cut so the dark image
             melts into black. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="ts-hero-glass">
            <div class="ts-hero-stage">
              <img class="ts-hero-shot is-active" data-shot="0" src="{{ 'tonescan-hero.png' | asset_url }}" alt="toneScan Develop view converting an RGB triplet scan" width="2000" height="1180" loading="eager">
              <div class="ts-hero-shot" data-shot="1"><span>[ RGB workflow ]</span></div>
              <div class="ts-hero-shot" data-shot="2"><span>[ Real-time editing ]</span></div>
              <div class="ts-hero-shot" data-shot="3"><span>[ Batch &amp; export ]</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} SELECTOR — sits on the black region below the cut. Desktop: tab pills.
       Mobile: pagination dots + a native <select>. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ts-hero-selectbar tw:relative tw:z-[2] tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1320px] tw:px-[15px] tw:md:px-[50px]">
      <div class="ts-hero-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Features">
        <button type="button" class="ts-hero-tab is-active" data-tab="0" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Develop</button>
        <button type="button" class="ts-hero-tab" data-tab="1" role="tab" aria-selected="false">RGB workflow</button>
        <button type="button" class="ts-hero-tab" data-tab="2" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Real-time editing</button>
        <button type="button" class="ts-hero-tab" data-tab="3" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Batch &amp; export</button>
      </div>
      <div class="ts-hero-mobsel">
        <div class="ts-hero-dots" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="ts-hero-dot is-active" data-dot="0"></span>
          <span class="ts-hero-dot" data-dot="1"></span>
          <span class="ts-hero-dot" data-dot="2"></span>
          <span class="ts-hero-dot" data-dot="3"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="ts-hero-selectwrap">
          <select class="ts-hero-select" aria-label="Choose a feature to preview">
            <option value="0">Develop</option>
            <option value="1">RGB workflow</option>
            <option value="2">Real-time editing</option>
            <option value="3">Batch &amp; export</option>
          </select>
          <svg class="ts-hero-selectcaret" viewBox="0 0 12 8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 1.5 6 6.5 11 1.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ==================== MARQUEE (scanned with tonescan) ====================
       Auto-scrolling strip of sample scans. Placeholders reuse existing images — swap
       scan_imgs for real converted scans later.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="tw:overflow-hidden tw:border-b tw:border-white/10 tw:py-[36px] tw:md:py-[44px]">
    <p class="tw:mb-[24px] tw:text-center tw:text-[13px] tw:font-semibold tw:uppercase tw:tracking-[0.16em] tw:text-[#60a5fa]">Scanned with tonescan</p>
    <div class="ts-marquee">
      <div class="ts-marquee__track">
        {%- assign scan_imgs = 'converted.jpg,raw-red.jpg,raw-green.jpg,converted.jpg,raw-blue.jpg,raw-green.jpg' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- for pass in (1..2) -%}
          {%- for f in scan_imgs -%}
            <div class="ts-marquee__item" style="background-image:url('{{ f | asset_url }}')"{% if pass == 2 %} aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}></div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ==================== 2 · SOCIAL PROOF STRIP ==================== {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="tw:border-y tw:border-white/10">
    <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:px-[15px] tw:py-[28px] tw:md:px-[50px]">
      <p class="tw:text-center tw:text-[14px] tw:text-neutral-500">
        From the team behind <span class="tw:text-neutral-300">toneCarrier</span> — trusted by hundreds of film photographers worldwide.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ==================== 3 · PROBLEM / AGITATION ==================== {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:px-[15px] tw:py-[80px] tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:py-[120px]">
    <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:max-w-[720px] tw:text-center">
      <p class="tw:mb-[16px] tw:text-[13px] tw:font-semibold tw:uppercase tw:tracking-[0.16em] tw:text-[#60a5fa]">The problem</p>
      <h2 class="tw:text-[32px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.1] tw:tracking-[-0.02em] tw:text-white tw:md:text-[46px]">
        Converting film shouldn't be the hard part.
      </h2>
      <p class="tw:mx-auto tw:mt-[20px] tw:max-w-[560px] tw:text-[17px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-neutral-400">
        You shot the roll. You scanned it. Then the fun stops — wrestling with clunky
        tools, chasing accurate colour, and fighting for consistency frame to frame.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="tw:mt-[48px] tw:grid tw:grid-cols-1 tw:gap-[16px] tw:md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[28px]">
        <div class="tw:mb-[14px] tw:h-[36px] tw:w-[36px] tw:rounded-[2px] tw:bg-white/10"></div>
        <h3 class="tw:mb-[8px] tw:text-[18px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Slow and fiddly</h3>
        <p class="tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.55] tw:text-neutral-400">Endless sliders and plugins just to get one frame looking right.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[28px]">
        <div class="tw:mb-[14px] tw:h-[36px] tw:w-[36px] tw:rounded-[2px] tw:bg-white/10"></div>
        <h3 class="tw:mb-[8px] tw:text-[18px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Inconsistent results</h3>
        <p class="tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.55] tw:text-neutral-400">Every frame comes out looking different from the last.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[28px]">
        <div class="tw:mb-[14px] tw:h-[36px] tw:w-[36px] tw:rounded-[2px] tw:bg-white/10"></div>
        <h3 class="tw:mb-[8px] tw:text-[18px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Hours per roll</h3>
        <p class="tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.55] tw:text-neutral-400">Manual tweaking and exporting turns a hobby into a chore.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ==================== 4 · INTERACTIVE DEMO ==================== {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="tw:relative tw:overflow-hidden tw:border-y tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.015]">
    <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:px-[15px] tw:py-[80px] tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:py-[120px] tw:text-center">
      <p class="tw:mb-[16px] tw:text-[13px] tw:font-semibold tw:uppercase tw:tracking-[0.16em] tw:text-[#60a5fa]">See it work</p>
      <h2 class="tw:mx-auto tw:max-w-[720px] tw:text-[32px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.1] tw:tracking-[-0.02em] tw:text-white tw:md:text-[46px]">
        Drag to reveal the conversion.
      </h2>
      <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:mt-[40px] tw:max-w-[920px]">
        {%- comment -%}
          Before/after slider. Placeholder gradients now; drop real scans in later by
          replacing the two .ts-ba__img divs with <img> (after = positive, before = negative)
          and removing .ts-ba__img--neg. Driven by a hidden range input (keyboard-accessible).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="ts-ba" style="--pos:50%">
          <div class="ts-ba__layer ts-ba__after"><div class="ts-ba__img"></div></div>
          <div class="ts-ba__layer ts-ba__before"><div class="ts-ba__img ts-ba__img--neg"></div></div>
          <div class="ts-ba__divider">
            <div class="ts-ba__handle" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 6 3 12l6 6M15 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="ts-ba__tag ts-ba__tag--l">Negative</span>
          <span class="ts-ba__tag ts-ba__tag--r">Converted</span>
          <input class="ts-ba__range" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Reveal the converted image">
        </div>
        <p class="tw:mt-[16px] tw:text-[13px] tw:text-neutral-500">Drag the handle to compare.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ==================== 5 · PLATFORM (bento) ====================
       Framer-style "full platform" bento. RGB is the hero tile.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section id="features" class="tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:scroll-mt-[84px] tw:px-[15px] tw:py-[80px] tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:py-[120px]">
    <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:max-w-[760px] tw:text-center">
      <p class="tw:mb-[16px] tw:text-[13px] tw:font-semibold tw:uppercase tw:tracking-[0.16em] tw:text-[#60a5fa]">The platform</p>
      <h2 class="tw:text-[32px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.1] tw:tracking-[-0.02em] tw:text-white tw:md:text-[46px]">
        A complete film workflow — not a plugin.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="tw:mt-[48px] tw:grid tw:grid-cols-1 tw:gap-[16px] tw:md:grid-cols-3 tw:md:auto-rows-[210px]">
      {%- comment -%} HERO tile: RGB {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="tw:flex tw:flex-col tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[28px] tw:md:col-span-2 tw:md:row-span-2">
        <div class="tw:mb-[22px] tw:flex tw:min-h-[180px] tw:flex-1 tw:items-center tw:justify-center tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-neutral-900 tw:text-[13px] tw:text-neutral-600">[ RGB channel visual ]</div>
        <h3 class="tw:text-[22px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Seamless RGB scanning</h3>
        <p class="tw:mt-[8px] tw:max-w-[460px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.55] tw:text-neutral-400">One of the only apps with clean, first-class support for RGB trichromatic capture — separate red, green and blue exposures combined for purer colour and none of the crosstalk of white light.</p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} small tiles {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="tw:flex tw:flex-col tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[24px]">
        <div class="tw:mb-[16px] tw:flex tw:h-[40px] tw:w-[40px] tw:items-center tw:justify-center tw:rounded-[2px] tw:bg-[#3b82f6]/15"><div class="tw:h-[16px] tw:w-[16px] tw:rounded-[1px] tw:bg-[#3b82f6]"></div></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Instant previews</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:text-[14px] tw:leading-[1.5] tw:text-neutral-400">Real-time GPU viewport — what you see is what you export.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tw:flex tw:flex-col tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[24px]">
        <div class="tw:mb-[16px] tw:flex tw:h-[40px] tw:w-[40px] tw:items-center tw:justify-center tw:rounded-[2px] tw:bg-[#3b82f6]/15"><div class="tw:h-[16px] tw:w-[16px] tw:rounded-[1px] tw:bg-[#3b82f6]"></div></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Automatic batch</h3>
